<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch central bank allocates fresh liquidity.</title>
<headline>Dutch central bank allocates fresh liquidity.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch central bank said on Thursday it allocated 3.05 billion guilders to the money market under an eight-day special advances pact at an unchanged rate of 2.90 percent.</p>
<p>Individual banks' applications up to 3.50 billion guilders were met for 12 percent. Above that level no subscriptions were awarded.</p>
<p>The pact replaces a six-day facility of 2.85 billion guilders which expired today.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsdesk +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
